# Project Portfolio & Earned Value Management (EVM) Dashboard

### Power BI | Project Controls | Portfolio Analytics | Financial Performance

## Project Overview

Developed an interactive Power BI dashboard using real-world enterprise project data to support project portfolio monitoring, financial performance analysis, and project controls.

The solution provides both **portfolio-level reporting** and **individual project performance analysis**, enabling management to monitor project progress, budgets, costs, schedule deviations, and overall project health.

## Key Features

**1. Project Portfolio Overview**
- Portfolio-wide monitoring of project progress and financial performance.
- Comparison of planned versus actual progress across multiple projects.
- Analysis of approved budgets, actual expenditures, and committed costs.
- Project distribution by actual completion percentage.
- Identification of schedule deviations and underperforming projects.
- Interactive project-level reporting and filtering.

**2. Earned Value Management (EVM)**
- Budget at Completion (BAC)
- Planned Value (PV)
- Earned Value (EV)
- Actual Cost (AC)
- Cost Variance (CV) and Schedule Variance (SV)
- Cost Performance Index (CPI) and Schedule Performance Index (SPI)
- Estimate at Completion (EAC) and Estimate to Complete (ETC)

**3. Project Schedule & Progress Analysis**
- Planned versus actual progress S-Curves.
- Project milestone tracking.
- Phase-level progress monitoring.
- Schedule variance identification.
- Planned and actual start and finish date comparisons.

**4. Risk & Financial Reporting**
- Project risk monitoring and assessment.
- Budget and expenditure trends.
- Cumulative financial performance analysis.
- Multi-currency financial reporting.

## Business Value

The dashboard was designed to support data-driven project governance by:

- Consolidating project performance information into a centralized reporting environment.
- Improving visibility into project cost and schedule performance.
- Supporting early identification of budget overruns and schedule delays.
- Enabling management to compare projects and prioritize corrective actions.
- Providing actionable insights through project-level and portfolio-level reporting.

